From: RK3308BS Armbian <build@armbian.local>
Date: Mon, 07 Sep 2026 08:24:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] input: touchscreen: add Rockchip vendor gt9xx driver (RK3308BS)

Port of the Rockchip vendor gt9xx driver (armbian/linux-rockchip
rk-6.1-rkr7.2) to kernel 6.18 for the RK3308BS M1SOC Goodix GT911.

6.18 fixes: hrtimer_setup, single-arg .probe, of_get_named_gpio, quoted
MODULE_IMPORT_NS, minimal tp_suspend.h stub. GTP_DRIVER_SEND_CFG=0 (use
the chip's own config). gtp_dat_gt11 = factory 1080x1920 blob.

RK3308BS_FOLD_FIX: this digitizer reports the horizontal axis (post-swap
ABS_MT_POSITION_Y) in a folded double-width space with a hard dead gap
[350..749]; two reachable bands [50..349] and [750..1079]. Unfold to a
clean 0..629; normalise the linear vertical axis (588..1741) to 0. Fixes
both the coordinate warp and the center phantom double-touch. Measured
from 700+ sample edge-to-edge drags; validated live via uinput remapper.
---
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/Kconfig b/drivers/input/touchscreen/Kconfig
index 7d5b72ee07fa..c4c6b628f5ae 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/Kconfig
@@ -1424,4 +1424,11 @@ config TOUCHSCREEN_HIMAX_HX83112B
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
 	  module will be called himax_hx83112b.
 
+config TOUCHSCREEN_GT9XX
+	tristate "Goodix gt9xx (vendor) support for rockchip platform"
+	depends on I2C
+	help
+	  Rockchip vendor gt9xx touchscreen driver (GT911/GT9271 etc).
+	  Ported from armbian/linux-rockchip for RK3308BS M1SOC.
+
 endif
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/Makefile b/drivers/input/touchscreen/Makefile
index ab9abd151078..d9cc632a48aa 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/Makefile
@@ -120,3 +120,4 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_IQS5XX)	+= iqs5xx.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_IQS7211)	+= iqs7211.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_ZINITIX)	+= zinitix.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_HIMAX_HX83112B)	+= himax_hx83112b.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_GT9XX)	+= gt9xx/
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/gt9xx/2059-V1-1024X600.cfg b/drivers/input/touchscreen/gt9xx/2059-V1-1024X600.cfg
new file mode 100755
